format 1
adapter feed 1
npc: npc-sage

post ft-sage-chest-daily
kind: celebrate
trigger: chest_opened
chip: quests
condition: {"period":"daily"}

text:
    A daily chest, opened. A small reward. Worth asking what small, steady habits add up to over a month.

post ft-sage-chest-weekly
kind: celebrate
trigger: chest_opened
chip: quests
condition: {"period":"weekly"}

text:
    The weekly chest is open. A week of quests, finished. Effort and patience both counted here.

post ft-sage-first-lesson
kind: celebrate
trigger: first_lesson
chip: lesson

text:
    Your first lesson is done: “{lesson}”. A good beginning. What question did it leave you with?

post ft-sage-quests
kind: celebrate
trigger: daily_quests_done
chip: quests

text:
    Every daily quest is claimed. A full day. Weigh it fairly: you did a lot, and the chest is waiting.

post ft-sage-rank-passed
kind: celebrate
trigger: rank_change
chip: ranks
condition: {"direction":"passed"}

text:
    You passed {rival} in the weekly ranking. A fair result. It is also worth asking what you learned on the way.

post ft-sage-comeback-14
kind: nudge
trigger: comeback
condition: {"minDays":14}

text:
    Welcome back, {name}. A pause is not a failure. When you are ready, one lesson is enough to see where you stand.

post ft-sage-comeback-3
kind: nudge
trigger: comeback
condition: {"minDays":3}

text:
    Welcome back, {name}. Whenever you are ready, the lessons are where you left them.

post ft-sage-rank-passed-by
kind: nudge
trigger: rank_change
chip: ranks
condition: {"direction":"passed_by"}

text:
    {rival} passed you in the weekly ranking. On one hand, that stings a little. On the other, one lesson can change it.
